  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 943 PM CST WED NOV 18 2026\n\nA slow moving upper-level trough will linger over the Deep South\nand Gulf through Friday, before merging with a disturbance near\nthe Bahamas on Saturday. This pattern will favor moistening\neasterly surface to 700 mb flow, resulting in increased\ncloudiness across the region and a few showers across southern\nAlabama through Friday. As the upper trough becomes entangled\nwith a disturbance near the Bahamas on Saturday, a coastal low is \nexpected to form over the Gulf Stream waters north of the Bahamas.\nSubsidence around the western side of this system will produce \nfewer clouds and dry conditions on Saturday across Alabama.\n\nA relatively weak front is expected to arrive Sunday night into\nMonday as a weakening shortwave traverses the region, but\nisentropic lift may be sufficient for an area of light rain along\nand behind the cold front. Predictability decreases after Monday \ndue to model disagreement which is a common symptom of a synoptic \npattern plagued by split flow and numerous small shortwaves.\n\n87/Grantham",
